## Overview

Diagnosed and resolved a persistent online connectivity issue affecting access to public gaming servers by systematically isolating network layers and identifying ISP-level configuration as the root cause.

## Components

Target Service    | Online Game Servers (Rust)
Network Layer     | Home Network + ISP Routing
Issue Type        | Inbound/Outbound Connectivity Failure
Root Cause        | CGNAT (Carrier-Grade NAT)
Resolution        | Static Public IP Assignment

## Process

Started troubleshooting by testing local system settings, game files, router configuration, and port-related assumptions. Gradually eliminated local causes through structured testing. Extended diagnosis to ISP-level networking after confirming no issues on the home network. Identified CGNAT as the limiting factor preventing stable server connectivity. Contacted ISP and requested a change from CGNAT to a static public IP. Verified successful resolution after network update restored full server access.

